<title>USA: Vons poised to leap, Safeway seen down.</title>
<headline>Vons poised to leap, Safeway seen down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vons Cos Inc shares are positioned to trade sharply higher Wednesday while Safeway Inc is poised to fall when the New York Stock Exchange lifts a trading halt on the stocks.</p>
<p>The NYSE halted trade in the stocks after Safeway offered to acquire the roughly two-thirds of Vons it does not own in a stock swap deal valuing Vons more than $58 per share.</p>
<p>The NYSE said the Vons quote was 50 bid, 53 ask, up from 43-1/8 while Safeway was indicated at 41-1/2 bid, 42-1/2 ask, off from 43-3/8.</p>
</text>
